WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.787
Each thread reads one x and one y value

00:00:03.787 --> 00:00:06.343
from GPU memory and computes a local

00:00:06.343 --> 00:00:06.708
intermediate.

00:00:11.208 --> 00:00:13.326
The temporary path writes the intermediate

00:00:13.326 --> 00:00:15.798
and reads it back. How many temporary

00:00:15.798 --> 00:00:17.916
reads and writes disappear for eight

00:00:17.916 --> 00:00:18.269
threads?

00:00:26.769 --> 00:00:29.379
Keeping the value local removes eight

00:00:29.379 --> 00:00:31.989
temporary writes and eight temporary reads

00:00:31.989 --> 00:00:34.599
in this source-level count. Compiler and

00:00:34.599 --> 00:00:36.774
cache behavior affect measured traffic.
